WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.264 --> 00:00:03.601
-My first guest is a multiple
Grammy-nominated artist

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:06.968
and one of the most talented
people on the planet.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:10.300
Her new album, "Dancing With the
Devil: The Art of Starting Over"

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.534
is out now.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.200
And her documentary
"Demi Lovato:

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.634
Dancing With the Devil"
is streaming on YouTube.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.734
Here's my BFF.
I love her.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.000
Demi Lovato!

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.133
[ Laughs ] That's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:24.133
Yeah! Come on.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:26.567
I'm so happy you're here.

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:28.767
-I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.400
-Oh, you look great, bud.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.901
Oh, before we get into it too,
I thought you were fantastic

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.234
at the inauguration --

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.300
-Thank you.
-...doing "Lovely Day."

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.968
That was -- Knock out.
That was one of my favorites.

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.501
The last time
you were on the show,

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.067
we were talking about
what you're into.

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:44.934
And you were saying that
you were into painting,

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.167
and we did portraits
of each other.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.167
-Yes.
-Do you remember this?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:48.667
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.300
-And I think I did okay.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.100
Here was my portrait
I did of you.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.501
-[ Chuckles ]
-Do you remember this?

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:58.367
-Yeah. Oh, yeah. Killer.
Really, really good.

00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:01.968
-I stopped at -- I didn't think
could I master the eyes.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:04.200
Cause, you know --

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.033
-I should have taken a note.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.400
-No, I just thought your eyes,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.901
they're too pretty
for me to paint.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.133
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.834
-And I did get a lot of hate,
by the way --

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.300
a little hate
for my name being so large.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.234
I don't know how to do -- sign.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.701
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:19.868
-I signed it really big.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.901
But then your portrait of me,
I thought was --

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.400
I thought it was pretty good.
I liked this, actually.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:24.767
This is --

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:26.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.267
[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.667
I thought it was fantastic.

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.100
I was thinking of, like,
sending it to you.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.400
And then I go, "Well, you're not
going to hang up

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.868
a portrait of yourself."

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:37.400
So I don't know what really
to do with it, but I would -- -

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.767
-Jimmy, if you sent it to me,

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.901
I would absolutely hang it up
in my house.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.200
-You would?

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.701
-Yes, absolutely.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.834
You painted a portrait of me.
How could I not?

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.400
-Okay. Very good. Alright.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.701
Then I'm going to send it
to you. Alright.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:52.367
Next time you come on, I want to
see it hanging somewhere.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.234
Pal, I want to talk about your
album, "Dancing With the Devil."

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.534
It is fantastic, by the way.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:58.701
-Thank you.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.200
-Really, it's unbelievable.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.400
'Cause the documentary --
I watched it,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.467
and I'm just not
going to get emotional,

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.400
but it is rough and tough.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.734
You know, I love you, and good
for you for doing this thing.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:16.434
And was it odd to go that honest
about your life

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:19.934
and talk about your life
straight to camera

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.901
and tell every single secret?

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.467
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:27.267
It was very --

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:28.367
It was challenging

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:31.033
because everything
that I went through

00:02:31.033 --> 00:02:35.334
in that storytelling journey
of making a documentary

00:02:35.334 --> 00:02:36.634
was difficult.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:40.367
And I had to work through
a lot of those things

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:44.868
before I actually
told the story on camera.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:48.868
But I've been working on,
you know, my --

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.501
I've been working on myself

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.601
and putting in a lot of work
behind the scenes

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:56.300
so that when it was time
to put it on camera,

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.634
I felt completely secure
in telling my story.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:02.868
And it's been really cathartic,
really, really therapeutic.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:07.367
And I'm just hoping that
a lot of people can learn

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.567
from what I went through

00:03:09.567 --> 00:03:12.868
and also, you know,

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:18.100
create conversation
around those topics.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:21.200
-Yeah. It already is.
It already is happening.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.901
Have you --
Have you watched this,

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:26.100
or can you even watch this
or no?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:32.133
-So, I watched it when the,
like, first cut was ready.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:38.100
Since then, I've seen it,
like, three or four times maybe.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.701
But, yeah, it was challenging.
It was challenging.

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.300
I had, like, a physical reaction

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.534
the first time
that I watched it,

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.234
like, anxiety attack.

00:03:45.234 --> 00:03:49.133
But -- But it's been --
it's been good.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:54.467
And a part of, you know, telling
my story is taking ownership.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.300
-Yeah.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.000
-And not --
And just owning my truth.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.334
No matter what people say
when they watch it,

00:04:03.334 --> 00:04:04.534
it doesn't matter.

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:05.868
And listen to my album.

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:08.100
Whatever people think
when they listen to my album,

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.400
I am so excited
about these two projects,

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.133
and I'm standing in such truth

00:04:14.133 --> 00:04:17.534
that nothing that anyone
can say can shake me.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.133
-What a record, by the way.

00:04:19.133 --> 00:04:20.300
What an album.
-Thank you.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.968
-It's unbelievable.

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:23.567
Obviously, I love
the title track,

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.167
"Dancing With the Devil."

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.367
Just knocked it out of the park.

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.634
It is fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:28.634
-I'm going to tell you
something.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.901
I don't know if you know this.

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:32.934
It is the biggest female
pop album debut of the year.

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:34.434
Congrats on that.
-That's good.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.300
-That's what I'm talking about.
That's what I'm talking about!

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.567
See what I'm talking about, pal?

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:38.801
Come on!

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:40.567
That's what I'm talking about!

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.334
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.834
Also, you know what I love?

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:48.634
I love that jam, I love --
I love a lot of them.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:51.200
I like "Met Him Last Night"
with Ariana Grande.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:55.501
-So Ariana and I have known
each other for several years.

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:59.167
And when she first came out
with her song, "The Way,"

00:04:59.167 --> 00:05:01.200
years ago, I heard that
and was like,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:05.234
"This girl is such a vocalist."

00:05:05.234 --> 00:05:06.634
And I'm such a fan.

00:05:06.634 --> 00:05:10.434
So we met,
and ever since that day,

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:13.234
we've talked about
wanting to do a song together.

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:16.801
But, you know,
it just never happened.

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.133
And she's just been someone

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:22.133
that's been really,
really supportive of my career.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.734
But when it came time
for this album,

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:24.834
I played her some of the songs.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.133
I played her
"Dancing With the Devil."

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:29.234
And she started writing
this song with me in mind,

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:32.300
and she played it for me
and, you know, she was like,

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.601
"I have this song.

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:36.868
I'm want to help
share your story."

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.133
And I was like, "You sound
incredible on this.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.567
You should stay on it,
and we can finally do

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.534
the song that we've always
wanted to do together."

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:44.968
-Yeah.
-So she was like, "Are you sure?

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.400
I was just going to be, like,

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.100
mystery harmony
background lady."

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.267
And I was like,

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.000
"No, you're Ariana."
-No, you're not. Yeah.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.868
-"Let's sing. Let's go."
-Everyone will know it's you.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.767
Yeah, exactly.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:55.934
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.133
It's fantastic, bud.
Congrats on this.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:05:59.734
I want to talk more
and maybe play

00:05:59.734 --> 00:06:01.567
a fun game with you
when we come back.

00:06:01.567 --> 00:06:02.701
-Yes.
-But, first, I wanted to

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.033
show everyone a clip.
Here's a peek at

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.234
"Demi Lovato: Dancing With
the Devil" on YouTube.

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:07.501
Take a look.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.667
-I remember
being in my hospital bed

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.400
and thinking, "Alright.
How do I fix this?

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.501
How do I get back to doing what
I love, which is making music?"

00:06:17.501 --> 00:06:19.567
-Demi is an honest songwriter.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.801
A lot of people are nervous
about telling everything.

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:25.968
Demi thrives on using her music
in a cathartic way.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.734
-I feel, like, with "Anyone,"
I knew that was a song

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.300
that I wanted to release
coming out of all of this.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.968
Because I thought if I ever
make it back to the stage,

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:37.334
I want to sing this song.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:39.634
-Yeah, that's what
I'm talking about, bud!

